# DTF tier manifest: storage-gc-bounded-deletes
#   artifact-keeper#2524 (1.12.0): storage GC no longer holds a database
#   transaction across an object-store delete, and a pass can be budgeted.
#
# Profile-set: s3 (MinIO) + storage.s3-slow-delete (new: a stdlib-python
# pass-through in front of MinIO that, once armed, holds the next N object
# deletes, single-object DELETE or multi-object POST ?delete, for a fixed
# time) + gc.storage-budget (new: STORAGE_GC_MAX_KEYS_PER_RUN=500, and
# GC_SCHEDULE once a year so no scheduled tick runs between the oracle's
# passes).
#
# THE CHANGE
# Before #2524 the orphan-key sweep re-checked each key under a per-key
# `FOR UPDATE` transaction and deleted the object INSIDE it: while the object
# store answered, the session sat `idle in transaction` holding row locks and
# a pooled connection, and one pass reclaimed every eligible key however many
# there were. Since #2524 a short transaction claims the key (re-check, hard
# delete of the soft-deleted rows, a journal row in oci_gc_candidates) and
# commits; the object delete runs afterwards with nothing held. New per-pass
# budgets STORAGE_GC_MAX_KEYS_PER_RUN / _BYTES_ / _RUN_SECS stop a pass early
# and report `budget_exhausted` ("keys", "bytes", "time") in the GC result,
# a dry run applies the same budget, and ak_storage_gc_budget_stops_total
# counts the stops.
#
# THE PRIMITIVES
#   One hosted generic repository. Three artifacts uploaded through the API
#   and deleted through the API (real objects in MinIO; content-addressed
#   hex keys, so they sort first and fall in the first pass), one live
#   artifact, and 2000 soft-deleted rows seeded with SQL (distinct keys
#   `zz-dtf-gc-<run>/<n>`, size_bytes 1024, deleted_at two days ago, no
#   object: a delete of a missing key succeeds on S3). Passes are driven
#   with POST /api/v1/admin/storage-gc. During the first live pass the shim
#   holds the first 8 deletes for 1.5 s each, and one psql session in the
#   postgres container samples pg_stat_activity every ~50 ms for sessions
#   `idle in transaction` for more than 100 ms.
#
# THE GATES (RED ak-backend:1.11.5, GREEN on the #2524 image)
#   (CONTROL)  both images: the uploaded-then-deleted objects are gone from
#              MinIO and their rows are gone after the pass that claimed
#              them; the live artifact downloads byte-exact after every pass.
#   (FIX)      inside the held-delete window no sample shows a session idle
#              in transaction (1.11.5: about 9 of 10 samples do, the
#              is_still_orphan FOR UPDATE query, for the whole 12 s window);
#              pass 1 reports 1..500 keys, budget_exhausted="keys", and the
#              soft-deleted row count drops by exactly what it reported
#              (1.11.5: 2003 keys, field absent, 0 rows left), and bytes_freed
#              is at least 1024 per key (1.11.5: 0, a NUMERIC sum read as
#              an integer); pass 2
#              reclaims the next 1..500 with budget_exhausted="keys"
#              (1.11.5: 0); a dry run before pass 1 reports 1..500 and leaves
#              the row count unchanged (1.11.5: 2003);
#              ak_storage_gc_budget_stops_total{budget="keys"} >= 1.
#   The idle-in-transaction gate needs the shim to have held all 8 deletes
#   and at least 10 samples inside the window; otherwise it is INFRA (the
#   pass did not go through the shim as set up), never a pass.
#
# Wall clock: about 2.5 min on 1.11.5 (one pass deletes all 2003 keys one
# at a time through the shim), less on the fix image.
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: not under test.
PROFILES="storage.s3 storage.s3-slow-delete gc.storage-budget"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
